# TV scope — supported tabs only

On **TV profile** (`ShellInputPolicy.tv`), only these shell tabs are in scope for UX, D-pad QA, and feature work. Do not spend TV polish on other tabs unless the user explicitly expands scope.

| Tab (user) | Nav ID | Primary screen |
|------------|--------|----------------|
| Home | `home` | `features/home/home_screen.dart` |
| Search | `search` | `features/search/search_screen.dart` |
| Anime | `anime` | `features/anime/anime_screen.dart` |
| Asian Drama | `asian_drama` | `features/asian_drama/asian_drama_screen.dart` |
| IPTV | `iptv` | `features/iptv/screens/iptv_pt_screen.dart` |
| Live Matches | `live_matches` | `features/live_matches/live_matches_screen.dart` |
| Lists | `mylist` | `features/my_list/my_list_screen.dart`, `lists_screen.dart` |
| Settings | `settings` | `features/settings/settings_screen.dart` |

Nav registry: `apps/forja/lib/shell/nav_config.dart` (`navDestinations`, `navTabBuilders`).

## Out of scope (TV) unless asked

`discover`, `similar`, `arabic`, `anime_arabic`, `books`, `music`, `comics`, `manga`, `jellyfin`, `downloader`, `magnet`, `audiobooks`.

## D-pad / focus checklist (in-scope pages)

Read `ShellScope.inputPolicyOf(context)` — never `ShellTokens.isTvLayout` in widgets.

| Pattern | When |
|---------|------|
| `shellFocusableTap` / `FocusableControl` | Cards, tiles, list rows, tappable catalog items |
| `ForjaInteractive` / `HeroPillPlayButton` + `FocusNode` | Hero CTAs; request initial focus when `policy.heroPlayAutoFocus` |
| `HubCinematicHero` | Shared hub hero (Anime, Asian Drama) — already wires TV autofocus |
| `ForjaShellChip` | Filter/mood chips (uses focus on TV automatically) |
| `HoverScale` | Delegates to `shellFocusableTap` on TV — prefer for legacy cards |
| `ExcludeFocus` on empty overlay | `shell_overlay_navigator.dart` — do not regress |
| **Text inputs / search fields** | **Browse focus only on D-pad land — never activate** (see below) |

Hub sub-routes pushed via `pushShellRoute` (details, search, explore) inherit the same rules.

## TV text inputs — focus ≠ activate (mandatory)

**Hard rule:** On TV, D-pad / arrow focus on a text field, search field, or search chrome control must **only move focus** (highlight). It must **never** open the keyboard, enter edit mode, expand search, submit, or fire `onTap` / `onSubmitted` / open handlers.

**Activate only on explicit select:** OK / Select / Enter / click / tap. Not on `onFocusChange(true)`, `autofocus`, or “focus landed so open it”.

| Do | Don’t |
|----|--------|
| Use `TvBrowseTextField` for TV search/query fields | Raw `TextField` that attaches IME when focused |
| Use browse/edit split like `SettingsTextField` (browse node in traversal; edit node only after OK) | `onFocusChange: (f) { if (f) openSearch() / beginEditing() }` |
| Open search chrome / keyboard from tool button `onTap` or activate key | Auto-open search or keyboard because focus moved onto Search / the field |
| Keep `readOnly` + no IME in browse; `TextInputType.none` until editing | `autofocus: true` on an editable field that pops the keyboard on land |

Canonical widgets: `shared/widgets/tv_browse_text_field.dart`, `SettingsTextField` in `settings_ui.dart`. Same contract for IPTV catalog search, portal search, hub search, player episode search, settings fields — every TV text input.

## Shell shared with all in-scope tabs

`shell_scaffold.dart`, `shell_nav_rail.dart`, `shell_overlay_navigator.dart`, `home_top_bar.dart`, `shared/tv/tv_remote_debug.dart`.

When fixing TV navigation on one in-scope tab, grep the same pattern across the other seven before marking done.
